    {
      "type": 1,
      "name": "notes",
      "content": {
        "json": "---\n**Notes:**\n- This workbook targets **Standard v2** APIM. The classic `Capacity` metric is not used: `CpuPercent_Gateway` / `MemoryPercent_Gateway` are the v2 equivalents and have no dimensions.\n- Platform metrics for `Requests`/`Duration`/`BackendDuration` support `ApiId`, `Hostname`, `Location`, `LastErrorReason`, and response-code(-category) dimensions - **not** `SubscriptionId`. There is no platform metric to see traffic per APIM subscription (i.e., per customer/PTU route chosen by subscription key). To validate that traffic lands on the intended PTU, either give each PTU its own API/backend in APIM (so the `ApiId` split above is a direct proxy), or emit subscription ID via an APIM policy (`azure-openai-emit-token-metric` / custom dimension) into Application Insights and query it there.\n- APIM's own metrics are gateway-side only: they show *that* the backend is slow/erroring, not *why*. Set the optional **Foundry / Azure OpenAI resource** parameter above to pull in Utilization V2, Active Tokens, and 429s directly on this page; or use the PTU validation workbook in the repo root for the full per-deployment breakdown."
      }
    }
